          "passage": "# Existing balcony planting options\n\nSynthetic planning notes for seeds and containers already on hand:\n\n- Option A uses one rectangular planter for thyme and chives. The packet labels describe thyme as needing a sunny position and chives as tolerating partial shade.\n- Option B uses two small pots for mint and parsley. The mint label recommends keeping it in its own pot; the parsley label allows partial shade.\n- A quick clear-day observation was estimated at about 4–5 hours of direct light on the balcony. It was an informal estimate, not a seasonal measurement.\n",
